+# Task contract — a coach stint with an end date beats an open copy
+
+objective: >
+  Issue #277, a defect in the pick that !450 merged: when one load carries a coach stint twice with
+  different end dates, the open copy wins, so a stint stays open after the coach has left. The latest
+  end date now wins, and an open copy only when no copy has an end.
+
+refs: >
+  #277 (plan approved in chat, 2026-11-09). Follows !450, whose build compared with prod showed the
+  defect.
+
+scope_paths:
+  - dbt_project/models/2_base/api_football/base_apif__coach_career.sql
+  - .claude/task/277-coach-end-date/contract.md
+  - .claude/task/277-coach-end-date/review.md
+  - .claude/task/277-coach-end-date/review_input.patch
+
+impact_map: >
+  writers: dbt only; no ingestion, seed or export change. base_apif__coach_career keeps its grain
+  and columns; only the order of its pick changes.
+  lineage: `dbt ls --resource-type model --output name --select base_apif__coach_career+` returns
+  2 models: base_apif__coach_career dim_coach_team_mapping. dim_coach_team_mapping feeds no model,
+  export or page.
+  consumption: none.
+  ci_layer_rules: scripts/check_layer_contract.py, scripts/check_description_hygiene.py.
+  deploy_order: one merge; the nightly rebuilds the two models. No backfill.
+  blast_radius: measured read-only by running the compiled model against prod's staging and
+  comparing it with the base_apif__coach_career built from 7bcdf434: 4 stints change, each to a later
+  end date (Bolivar 2020-12-01 to 2021-05-01, UAE 2019-03-01 to 2022-02-01, Pontevedra 2021-05-01 to
+  2021-06-01, Arosa open to 2024-06-01). Against !450's open-first order it also closes 3 stints that
+  order leaves open: Shkendija (the coach is at Qabala from 2026-10), Glentoran (at Dungannon Swifts
+  from 2023-06) and Reggiana (ended 2019-04).
+  recurring_cost: none; the model already runs nightly.
+
+approved_design:
+  - none: no page output changes
+
+decisions_taken: >
+  Under the approved #277 line "every row picked by an order holds a test that the order keys are
+  unique within the group": a coach stint takes the latest end date, open only when no copy has one,
+  then the team name. The pick stays total: every output column is a partition or order key.
+
+decisions_reserved:
+  - none: no metric, label or page composition changes.
+
+acceptance_criteria:
+  - Every row picked by an order holds a test that the order keys are unique within the group.
+
+done_when:
+  - dbt parse succeeds from the repo root.
+  - python scripts/check_layer_contract.py passes.
+  - python -m pytest tests -q is green.
+  - SQLFluff adds no violation on base_apif__coach_career.
+  - CI's data:build:mr is green, and base_apif__coach_career and dim_coach_team_mapping are compared with prod.
